From d90ac89290ba3c669a129cc38a9dbe1e0ebe0e82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 19:55:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Scaffold Nawa AI: Jordanian-Arabic voice backend for Vapi
 Custom LLM
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Production-ready FastAPI backend acting as a Custom LLM for Vapi.ai, built
around a sub-500ms time-to-first-token budget. Everything streams; guardrails
are regex-only (no second LLM on the live path).

- POST /chat/completions: OpenAI-format SSE (data: {…}\n\n, [DONE]) via
  StreamingResponse, X-Accel-Buffering: no, ensure_ascii=False for Arabic
- One app-wide AsyncOpenAI client; gpt-4o-mini via LLM_MODEL env (stream=True,
  temperature=0.3, max_tokens=250); lifespan warms LLM/Qdrant/Redis pools
- Input guard (regex/blocklist, <1ms) for injection/unsafe/off-topic; polite
  Jordanian redirect on block
- Sentence-level output guard during the stream (Arabic boundaries ، . ؟ ! \n):
  blocks fake promises, info leaks, invented prices; graceful fallback + [DONE],
  never dead air
- RAG: cached text-embedding-3-small, top-3 Qdrant with metadata prefilter,
  regex intent gate to skip chitchat, dedicated context system block
- Per-call state + embedding cache in Redis; structured logs with call_id + TTFT
- Strict Jordanian-Arabic system prompt for "نوا" with FEW_SHOT_EXAMPLES scaffold
- Dockerfile (slim py3.12, uvicorn+uvloop+httptools, single worker),
  docker-compose (app+qdrant+redis), ingest script, README with Vapi wiring and
  ECS Fargate deployment notes

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
